  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1212 AM CDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nAs of 12:30 AM CDT, temperatures across the region are in the \nupper 60s to low 70s with winds out of the northwest behind a cold \nfront and out of the southeast ahead of the cold front. Storms will \ncontinue to move across eastern SD for the next several hours and \nare expected to decrease in strength as they continue southeast.\n\nToday through Thursday is expected to have quiet, dry weather as \nhigh pressure moves into the region. Storm chances return Friday \nthrough the weekend but confidence on severe weather is low at this \ntime. Temperatures through the period are still expected to be \naround to slightly above average, warmest towards the weekend and \ncooling down into next work week. HRRR smoke shows some smoke move \ninto the forecast area today with some higher concentrations over \nnortheast SD. There could be a little bit of smoke at the surface \nlending a slight smoky smell to the air, but the higher \nconcentrations (still only a small amount) are expected Wednesday at \nthe surface. This isn't expected to reduce visibilities much at all, \nbut could give the air a smoky smell again. Winds Tuesday are \nexpected to gust up to 35 mph mainly across northern SD, but could \nreach as far south as Redfield or Highmore, SD.",
